        "VCC",
        "GND"
      ],
      "observed": "C8 is specified in the netlist and SPICE deck as a 100 pF capacitor connected between VCC and GND.",
      "expected": "The design specification lists C8 as one of the 100 nF local VCC-GND bypass capacitors.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C8\")\n      (value \"100p\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C8 VCC 0 100p"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C2, C3, C4, C5, C6, C8 — 100 nF each, VCC–GND (local bypass)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "This reduces the intended local decoupling capacitance by a factor of 1000 at that VCC-GND bypass location, which can increase supply noise and EMI and may affect stable operation of nearby circuits such as the NFC IC or display.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "An anomaly is detected: C8 is 100 pF in the design files but the specification requires it to be 100 nF as a VCC-GND bypass capacitor. The unresolved C18 value is a documented design limitation and is not reported as an anomaly."
}

